\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The register-choice phase diagram for $\gamma =1$ and $\eta =0.8$. Below $C_{\rm  crit}(\theta )$, splitting retains both tasks. Above it, the shared optimum is balanced at small $\theta $ and suppresses an evaluator at large $\theta $. Solid boundaries mark tied costs, including the vertical attention boundary above the meeting point. At that meeting point all shared attention weights are degenerate and splitting has the same cost. The dashed $C_{\rm  part}=0.25$ slice recovers Figure~\ref {fig:dd-shared-register-price}. The regions are the exact optima of the declared finite model.}}{4}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dd-register-phase-diagram}{{2}{4}{The register-choice phase diagram for $\gamma =1$ and $\eta =0.8$. Below $C_{\rm crit}(\theta )$, splitting retains both tasks. Above it, the shared optimum is balanced at small $\theta $ and suppresses an evaluator at large $\theta $. Solid boundaries mark tied costs, including the vertical attention boundary above the meeting point. At that meeting point all shared attention weights are degenerate and splitting has the same cost. The dashed $C_{\rm part}=0.25$ slice recovers Figure~\ref {fig:dd-shared-register-price}. The regions are the exact optima of the declared finite model}{figure.caption.2}{}}
