\newlabel{eq:four-state-memory}{{15}{7}{What a summary must remember}{equation.3.15}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Equal summaries, different futures. Exact region probabilities $p_A(t)$ for the four-state process, starting in state 1 or 2. The coarse model without the hidden imbalance $z$ predicts the same curve for both initial states. It initially lies between the exact trajectories but does not remain between them. Retaining $z$, or its exact memory kernel, recovers both trajectories. Time $t$ is in inverse base-rate units. The curves are analytic trajectories of Eq.~\eqref  {eq:four-state}.}}{7}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dd-retention-trajectories}{{4}{7}{Equal summaries, different futures. Exact region probabilities $p_A(t)$ for the four-state process, starting in state 1 or 2. The coarse model without the hidden imbalance $z$ predicts the same curve for both initial states. It initially lies between the exact trajectories but does not remain between them. Retaining $z$, or its exact memory kernel, recovers both trajectories. Time $t$ is in inverse base-rate units. The curves are analytic trajectories of Eq.~\eqref {eq:four-state}}{figure.caption.4}{}}
