\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The same optimum with different feedback. For the product-state example of Cerezo et al.~\cite  {Cerezo2021232f10}, the global and local losses in Eq.~\eqref  {eq:global-local-cost} have the same zero-cost target. With independent uniform angles, $\operatorname  {Var}(\partial _j C_G)=\tfrac  18(\tfrac  38)^{n-1}$, while $\operatorname  {Var}(\partial _j C_L)=1/(8n^2)$. Here $n$ is the number of qubits. Exact model variances isolate cost-dependent concentration.}}{16}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
