\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Retain the relation rather than its list of instances. (a) In the uniform three-bit even-parity law, each pair is independent but two bits determine the third. A running parity state represents the allowed continuations. (b) Archived timings for the 19-bit law with 262,144 distinct worlds, queries fixing four prefix coordinates and batch size $Q$. All displayed prefix queries have count 16,384. The plotted $t_{\rm  API}$ is warm full-API time per batch. Dots are all eleven samples and lines join medians. Build, query preparation and first-process compilation are excluded. The campaign also records capacity refusals and a duplicate-heavy control in which direct scan wins.}}{29}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dd-memory-parity}{{13}{29}{Retain the relation rather than its list of instances. (a) In the uniform three-bit even-parity law, each pair is independent but two bits determine the third. A running parity state represents the allowed continuations. (b) Archived timings for the 19-bit law with 262,144 distinct worlds, queries fixing four prefix coordinates and batch size $Q$. All displayed prefix queries have count 16,384. The plotted $t_{\rm API}$ is warm full-API time per batch. Dots are all eleven samples and lines join medians. Build, query preparation and first-process compilation are excluded. The campaign also records capacity refusals and a duplicate-heavy control in which direct scan wins}{figure.caption.13}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Where the language-memory implementation needs improvement. Archived LongMem answer counts with the same reader and a 4,000-token evidence budget. Memory, dense and hybrid retrieval answer 30, 33 and 34 of the 48 questions correctly. On the nine temporal questions the counts are 4, 7 and 6. The small temporal subset identifies concrete failures to investigate, rather than estimating a universal performance gap.}}{30}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dd-memory-reader-controls}{{14}{30}{Where the language-memory implementation needs improvement. Archived LongMem answer counts with the same reader and a 4,000-token evidence budget. Memory, dense and hybrid retrieval answer 30, 33 and 34 of the 48 questions correctly. On the nine temporal questions the counts are 4, 7 and 6. The small temporal subset identifies concrete failures to investigate, rather than estimating a universal performance gap}{figure.caption.14}{}}
